Grant of Rights

The Licensor hereby grants you the right to copy, modify, create derivative
works, redistribute, and make non-production use of the Licensed Work. The
Licensor also grants you the right to make production use of the Licensed Work,
provided that such use is not a Competing Use.

Competing Use

A "Competing Use" means making the Licensed Work available, directly or
indirectly, to third parties as a software-as-a-service, hosted service,
managed service, or any other service that substitutes for or competes with any
SusDevOS product or service offered by the Licensor.

Examples that are NOT a Competing Use (and are therefore permitted):
  - Running SusDevOS for your own organisation's internal GHG reporting
  - Self-hosting SusDevOS for a single client you are engaged by
  - Building integrations, connectors, or tooling on top of SusDevOS
  - Contributing to or forking SusDevOS for non-commercial or research purposes
  - Running SusDevOS in a test, staging, or development environment

Examples that ARE a Competing Use (and are therefore prohibited):
  - Operating a multi-tenant GHG/ESG reporting platform that uses SusDevOS
    code and charges customers for access
  - Reselling or white-labelling SusDevOS as a managed service to clients

